   "source": [
    "## Regression metrics\n",
    "- the target variable is continuous\n",
    "- the predicted values are also continuous\n",
    "- regression metrics measure some type of difference between y (true values) and y' (predicted values)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "subslide"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "### Mean Squared Error \n",
    "\n",
    "        \n",
    "$$MSE(y,y') = \\frac{1}{m}\\sum_{i=1}^{m}(y_i-y_i')^2$$\n",
    "\n",
    "<center><img src=\"../figures/polifit_1.jpg\" width=\"450\"></center>\n",
    "\n",
    "#### The unit of MSE is not the same as the target variable."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "subslide"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "### Root Mean Square Error\n",
    "\n",
    "$$RMSE(y,y') = \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{m}\\sum_{i=1}^{m}(y_i-y_i')^2}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "### Mean Absolute Error\n",
    "\n",
    "$$MAE(y,y') = \\frac{1}{m}\\sum_{i=1}^{m}|y_i-y_i'|$$\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Both RMSE and MAE have the same unit as the target variable.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": "subslide"
    }
   },
   "source": [
    "## R2 score - coefficient of determination\n",
    "\n",
    "$$R^2(y,y') = 1 - \\frac{\\sum_{i=1}^{m}(y_i-y_i')^2}{\\sum_{i=1}^{m}(y_i-\\bar{y})^2}$$\n",
    "where $\\bar{y}$ is the mean of $y$.\n",
    "\n",
    "- R2 = 1 is the perfect regression model ($y == y'$)\n",
    "- R2 = 0 is as good as a constant model that always predicts the expected value of y ($\\bar{y}$)\n",
    "- R2 < 0 is a bad regression model\n",
    "\n",
    "#### R2 is dimensionless."
   ]
  },
